According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global Real Time Location Systems in Sports (RTLS) Market was valued at USD 0.85 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 1.45 billion by 2034, growing at a robust CAGR of 6.1% during the forecast period (2025–2034). This growth is driven by the increasing penetration of data driven coaching tools across professional leagues, the rapid adoption of cloud native analytics in collegiate programs, and the expansion of fan engagement platforms that leverage real time positional data.
The RTLS market combines advanced ultra wideband (UWB), Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE), and radio frequency identification (RFID) technologies to deliver millisecond level positional accuracy. Such precision enables teams to refine tactics, monitor player loads, and reduce injury risk while broadcasters deliver immersive visualisations that enhance viewer experience. High stakes sports organisations now view RTLS as a core capability that delivers measurable on field performance improvements and off field commercial benefits.
